# infra/load-plans/baseline.nuon
#
# The broker's baseline (docs/architecture/policy-enforcement.md, stage 5a), before stage 5b changes it: every size at
# every rate, one producer and one sink on one lane. 16 runs. Each sends 20 seconds of messages at its rate (as fast as
# the window allows for a rate of 0), at most 100,000 messages and 1 GiB of payload per producer, the first 100 of each
# left out of the latencies.
#
# Four producers and four sinks on four lanes were in it, and were taken out (2026-10-21): the four producers are one
# workload, so one identity, and the broker lets an identity have one live session (a new one supersedes the others
# and closes their connections). Those runs measured the pods taking each other's sessions over, a reconnection a
# second, not the broker. Several connections at once need a distinct identity for each pod; until there is a way to
# give them that, the plan measures one.
#
#   nu infra/load-harness.nu run infra/load-plans/baseline.nuon
{
  name: "baseline"
  defaults: { seconds: 20, max_count: 100000, max_bytes: 1073741824, warmup: 100 }
  grid: {
    size: [256 4096 65536 1048576]
    rate: [100 1000 10000 0]
    shape: [
      { producers: 1, sinks: 1, lanes: 1 }
    ]
  }
}
